IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `amd-act`

-- Advance Medical Directive Act 1996 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING, not about the law: it fixes
-- what the rules answer on stated facts, so that a later change which alters an
-- answer is caught. Nothing here has been checked against a decided case or
-- against the prescribed forms.

§ `Fixtures`

`no interests` MEANS Interests WITH
    `a beneficiary under the patient's will or any policy of insurance` IS FALSE
    `has an interest under an instrument under which the patient is donor, settlor or grantor` IS FALSE
    `would be entitled to an interest in the estate on the patient's intestacy` IS FALSE
    `would be entitled to the patient's provident fund moneys on death` IS FALSE
    `has registered an objection under section 10(1)` IS FALSE

-- A person who takes on the patient's intestacy and nothing else. This is the
-- limb that s 3(3)(c) names and that ss 9(9) and 10(4) do not.
`only an intestacy entitlement` MEANS Interests WITH
    `a beneficiary under the patient's will or any policy of insurance` IS FALSE
    `has an interest under an instrument under which the patient is donor, settlor or grantor` IS FALSE
    `would be entitled to an interest in the estate on the patient's intestacy` IS TRUE
    `would be entitled to the patient's provident fund moneys on death` IS FALSE
    `has registered an objection under section 10(1)` IS FALSE

`a beneficiary under the will` MEANS Interests WITH
    `a beneficiary under the patient's will or any policy of insurance` IS TRUE
    `has an interest under an instrument under which the patient is donor, settlor or grantor` IS FALSE
    `would be entitled to an interest in the estate on the patient's intestacy` IS FALSE
    `would be entitled to the patient's provident fund moneys on death` IS FALSE
    `has registered an objection under section 10(1)` IS FALSE

`Tan, aged 70` MEANS Person WITH
    `name` IS "Tan"
    `age in years` IS 70
    `mentally disordered` IS FALSE

`Lim, aged 20` MEANS Person WITH
    `name` IS "Lim"
    `age in years` IS 20
    `mentally disordered` IS FALSE

`Wong, aged 45` MEANS Person WITH
    `name` IS "Wong"
    `age in years` IS 45
    `mentally disordered` IS FALSE

`Ng, aged 19` MEANS Person WITH
    `name` IS "Ng"
    `age in years` IS 19
    `mentally disordered` IS FALSE

`Dr Chua, the patient's own doctor` MEANS Witness WITH
    `who` IS `Wong, aged 45`
    `is a medical practitioner` IS TRUE
    `is the patient's own or chosen practitioner` IS TRUE
    `interests` IS `no interests`

`a lay witness aged 45` MEANS Witness WITH
    `who` IS `Wong, aged 45`
    `is a medical practitioner` IS FALSE
    `is the patient's own or chosen practitioner` IS FALSE
    `interests` IS `no interests`

`a lay witness aged 19` MEANS Witness WITH
    `who` IS `Ng, aged 19`
    `is a medical practitioner` IS FALSE
    `is the patient's own or chosen practitioner` IS FALSE
    `interests` IS `no interests`

`a lay witness who takes under the will` MEANS Witness WITH
    `who` IS `Wong, aged 45`
    `is a medical practitioner` IS FALSE
    `is the patient's own or chosen practitioner` IS FALSE
    `interests` IS `a beneficiary under the will`

§§ `3 -- who may make a directive`

#ASSERT `the person may make a directive` `Tan, aged 70`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may make a directive` `Lim, aged 20`

-- s 3(1) takes "has attained 21 years of age" as a bright line, so 21 passes
-- and 20 does not. The boundary is asserted because it is the whole of the
-- age test.
`Chan, aged exactly 21` MEANS Person WITH
    `name` IS "Chan"
    `age in years` IS 21
    `mentally disordered` IS FALSE

`Chan, mentally disordered` MEANS Person WITH
    `name` IS "Chan"
    `age in years` IS 40
    `mentally disordered` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `the person may make a directive` `Chan, aged exactly 21`
#ASSERT NOT `the person may make a directive` `Chan, mentally disordered`

§§ `3(2) -- the two witnesses, in either order`

`a directive properly witnessed` MEANS Directive WITH
    `the patient` IS `Tan, aged 70`
    `in the prescribed form` IS TRUE
    `first witness` IS `Dr Chua, the patient's own doctor`
    `second witness` IS `a lay witness aged 45`
    `the witnesses were present at the same time` IS TRUE
    `registered under section 5` IS TRUE
    `revoked under section 7` IS FALSE

-- The same two witnesses, swapped. s 3(2) does not say which is which, so the
-- answer must not depend on the order they are recorded in.
`the same directive, witnesses swapped` MEANS Directive WITH
    `the patient` IS `Tan, aged 70`
    `in the prescribed form` IS TRUE
    `first witness` IS `a lay witness aged 45`
    `second witness` IS `Dr Chua, the patient's own doctor`
    `the witnesses were present at the same time` IS TRUE
    `registered under section 5` IS TRUE
    `revoked under section 7` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the directive was made in accordance with section 3` `a directive properly witnessed`
#ASSERT `the directive was made in accordance with section 3` `the same directive, witnesses swapped`

-- Neither witness is the patient's own or chosen practitioner: s 3(2)(a) fails.
`a directive witnessed by two lay people` MEANS Directive WITH
    `the patient` IS `Tan, aged 70`
    `in the prescribed form` IS TRUE
    `first witness` IS `a lay witness aged 45`
    `second witness` IS `a lay witness aged 45`
    `the witnesses were present at the same time` IS TRUE
    `registered under section 5` IS TRUE
    `revoked under section 7` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the directive was made in accordance with section 3` `a directive witnessed by two lay people`

-- The second witness is 19: s 3(2)(b) fails.
`a directive witnessed by a 19 year old` MEANS Directive WITH
    `the patient` IS `Tan, aged 70`
    `in the prescribed form` IS TRUE
    `first witness` IS `Dr Chua, the patient's own doctor`
    `second witness` IS `a lay witness aged 19`
    `the witnesses were present at the same time` IS TRUE
    `registered under section 5` IS TRUE
    `revoked under section 7` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the directive was made in accordance with section 3` `a directive witnessed by a 19 year old`

-- A witness who takes under the will: s 3(3)(a) fails.
`a directive witnessed by a beneficiary` MEANS Directive WITH
    `the patient` IS `Tan, aged 70`
    `in the prescribed form` IS TRUE
    `first witness` IS `Dr Chua, the patient's own doctor`
    `second witness` IS `a lay witness who takes under the will`
    `the witnesses were present at the same time` IS TRUE
    `registered under section 5` IS TRUE
    `revoked under section 7` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the witness is competent under section 3(3)` `a lay witness who takes under the will`
#ASSERT NOT `the directive was made in accordance with section 3` `a directive witnessed by a beneficiary`

-- Not present at the same time: s 3(2) fails on its own words.
`a directive witnessed separately` MEANS Directive WITH
    `the patient` IS `Tan, aged 70`
    `in the prescribed form` IS TRUE
    `first witness` IS `Dr Chua, the patient's own doctor`
    `second witness` IS `a lay witness aged 45`
    `the witnesses were present at the same time` IS FALSE
    `registered under section 5` IS TRUE
    `revoked under section 7` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the directive was made in accordance with section 3` `a directive witnessed separately`

§§ `4 -- the duty that falls only on a medical witness`

`all four steps taken` MEANS WitnessingSteps WITH
    `satisfied that the patient is not mentally disordered` IS TRUE
    `satisfied that the patient has attained 21 years` IS TRUE
    `satisfied that the directive was made voluntarily and without inducement or compulsion` IS TRUE
    `satisfied that the patient was informed of the nature and consequences` IS TRUE

`nothing done` MEANS WitnessingSteps WITH
    `satisfied that the patient is not mentally disordered` IS FALSE
    `satisfied that the patient has attained 21 years` IS FALSE
    `satisfied that the directive was made voluntarily and without inducement or compulsion` IS FALSE
    `satisfied that the patient was informed of the nature and consequences` IS FALSE

-- The medical witness who does nothing contravenes s 4.
#ASSERT `the witness contravenes section 4` `Dr Chua, the patient's own doctor` `nothing done`
#ASSERT NOT `the witness contravenes section 4` `Dr Chua, the patient's own doctor` `all four steps taken`

-- The LAY witness who does nothing does not, because s 4 binds only "a witness
-- who is a medical practitioner". The pair is the point.
#ASSERT NOT `the witness contravenes section 4` `a lay witness aged 45` `nothing done`

§§ `9(4) -- the composition of the two second opinions`

`a specialist` MEANS MedicalPractitioner WITH
    `who` IS `Wong, aged 45`
    `is a specialist` IS TRUE
    `interests` IS `no interests`
    `has registered an objection under section 10(1)` IS FALSE

`a non-specialist` MEANS MedicalPractitioner WITH
    `who` IS `Wong, aged 45`
    `is a specialist` IS FALSE
    `interests` IS `no interests`
    `has registered an objection under section 10(1)` IS FALSE

-- (a) treating practitioner is NOT a specialist: both others must be.
#ASSERT `the second opinions answer section 9(4)` `a non-specialist` `a specialist` `a specialist`
#ASSERT NOT `the second opinions answer section 9(4)` `a non-specialist` `a specialist` `a non-specialist`

-- (b) treating practitioner IS a specialist: one of the others is enough.
#ASSERT `the second opinions answer section 9(4)` `a specialist` `a specialist` `a non-specialist`
#ASSERT NOT `the second opinions answer section 9(4)` `a specialist` `a non-specialist` `a non-specialist`

§§ `9(5)-(7) -- the committee, and the presumption against terminal illness`

`both opinions agree` MEANS Determination WITH
    `the treating practitioner` IS `a specialist`
    `the first opinion` IS `a specialist`
    `the second opinion` IS `a specialist`
    `the first opinion agrees` IS TRUE
    `the second opinion agrees` IS TRUE
    `the committee was unanimous that the patient is terminally ill` IS FALSE

`the opinions are split, committee unanimous` MEANS Determination WITH
    `the treating practitioner` IS `a specialist`
    `the first opinion` IS `a specialist`
    `the second opinion` IS `a specialist`
    `the first opinion agrees` IS TRUE
    `the second opinion agrees` IS FALSE
    `the committee was unanimous that the patient is terminally ill` IS TRUE

`the opinions are split, committee divided` MEANS Determination WITH
    `the treating practitioner` IS `a specialist`
    `the first opinion` IS `a specialist`
    `the second opinion` IS `a specialist`
    `the first opinion agrees` IS TRUE
    `the second opinion agrees` IS FALSE
    `the committee was unanimous that the patient is terminally ill` IS FALSE

-- Two agreeing opinions settle it without a committee.
#ASSERT NOT `the issue must be referred to a committee` `both opinions agree`
#ASSERT `the patient is determined to be terminally ill under section 9` `both opinions agree`

-- A split sends it to the committee, and only unanimity carries it.
#ASSERT `the issue must be referred to a committee` `the opinions are split, committee unanimous`
#ASSERT `the patient is determined to be terminally ill under section 9` `the opinions are split, committee unanimous`

-- s 9(7): a divided committee means the patient is PRESUMED NOT terminally ill.
-- This is the boundary case for the whole of Part 9 and the one that decides
-- whether treatment continues.
#ASSERT `the issue must be referred to a committee` `the opinions are split, committee divided`
#ASSERT NOT `the patient is determined to be terminally ill under section 9` `the opinions are split, committee divided`

§§ `10 -- the duty to act, and what lifts it`

`an objecting practitioner` MEANS MedicalPractitioner WITH
    `who` IS `Wong, aged 45`
    `is a specialist` IS TRUE
    `interests` IS `no interests`
    `has registered an objection under section 10(1)` IS TRUE

`a practitioner who takes under the will` MEANS MedicalPractitioner WITH
    `who` IS `Wong, aged 45`
    `is a specialist` IS TRUE
    `interests` IS `a beneficiary under the will`
    `has registered an objection under section 10(1)` IS FALSE

`a practitioner entitled only on intestacy` MEANS MedicalPractitioner WITH
    `who` IS `Wong, aged 45`
    `is a specialist` IS TRUE
    `interests` IS `only an intestacy entitlement`
    `has registered an objection under section 10(1)` IS FALSE

`the ordinary case` MEANS ActingSituation WITH
    `the directive` IS `a directive properly witnessed`
    `the determination` IS `both opinions agree`
    `the practitioner` IS `a specialist`
    `reasonable ground to believe a notice of revocation has been received or sent` IS FALSE
    `reasonable ground to believe the patient communicated an intention to revoke` IS FALSE
    `reasonable ground to believe the patient could not understand the directive when made` IS FALSE
    `ascertained from the Registrar that the directive is registered and in force` IS TRUE
    `ensured the patient has been certified terminally ill under section 9` IS TRUE
    `determined and certified whether the patient is pregnant` IS TRUE
    `the patient is known to the practitioner to be pregnant` IS FALSE
    `it is probable the foetus will develop to the point of live birth with continued treatment` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the practitioner has a duty to act in accordance with the directive` `the ordinary case`
#ASSERT `the practitioner may lawfully act on the directive` `the ordinary case`

-- s 10(2)(b): a communicated intention to revoke lifts the duty, even though
-- nothing has reached the register.
`the patient said he had changed his mind` MEANS ActingSituation WITH
    `the directive` IS `a directive properly witnessed`
    `the determination` IS `both opinions agree`
    `the practitioner` IS `a specialist`
    `reasonable ground to believe a notice of revocation has been received or sent` IS FALSE
    `reasonable ground to believe the patient communicated an intention to revoke` IS TRUE
    `reasonable ground to believe the patient could not understand the directive when made` IS FALSE
    `ascertained from the Registrar that the directive is registered and in force` IS TRUE
    `ensured the patient has been certified terminally ill under section 9` IS TRUE
    `determined and certified whether the patient is pregnant` IS TRUE
    `the patient is known to the practitioner to be pregnant` IS FALSE
    `it is probable the foetus will develop to the point of live birth with continued treatment` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the practitioner has a duty to act in accordance with the directive` `the patient said he had changed his mind`

-- s 10(1) with s 10(5): an objection lifts the duty and raises a duty to
-- transfer the patient's care instead.
`the practitioner objects` MEANS ActingSituation WITH
    `the directive` IS `a directive properly witnessed`
    `the determination` IS `both opinions agree`
    `the practitioner` IS `an objecting practitioner`
    `reasonable ground to believe a notice of revocation has been received or sent` IS FALSE
    `reasonable ground to believe the patient communicated an intention to revoke` IS FALSE
    `reasonable ground to believe the patient could not understand the directive when made` IS FALSE
    `ascertained from the Registrar that the directive is registered and in force` IS TRUE
    `ensured the patient has been certified terminally ill under section 9` IS TRUE
    `determined and certified whether the patient is pregnant` IS TRUE
    `the patient is known to the practitioner to be pregnant` IS FALSE
    `it is probable the foetus will develop to the point of live birth with continued treatment` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `the practitioner has a duty to act in accordance with the directive` `the practitioner objects`
#ASSERT `the practitioner must transfer the patient's care under section 10(5)` `the practitioner objects`
#ASSERT NOT `the practitioner must transfer the patient's care under section 10(5)` `the ordinary case`

-- s 10(4): a practitioner who takes under the will has a DUTY under s 10(2)
-- and is forbidden to act by s 10(4). The duty and the prohibition sit on the
-- same person at once; s 10(5) is what resolves it, by transfer.
`the practitioner takes under the will` MEANS ActingSituation WITH
    `the directive` IS `a directive properly witnessed`
    `the determination` IS `both opinions agree`
    `the practitioner` IS `a practitioner who takes under the will`
    `reasonable ground to believe a notice of revocation has been received or sent` IS FALSE
    `reasonable ground to believe the patient communicated an intention to revoke` IS FALSE
    `reasonable ground to believe the patient could not understand the directive when made` IS FALSE
    `ascertained from the Registrar that the directive is registered and in force` IS TRUE
    `ensured the patient has been certified terminally ill under section 9` IS TRUE
    `determined and certified whether the patient is pregnant` IS TRUE
    `the patient is known to the practitioner to be pregnant` IS FALSE
    `it is probable the foetus will develop to the point of live birth with continued treatment` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the practitioner has a duty to act in accordance with the directive` `the practitioner takes under the will`
#ASSERT NOT `the practitioner may lawfully act on the directive` `the practitioner takes under the will`
#ASSERT `the practitioner must transfer the patient's care under section 10(5)` `the practitioner takes under the will`

-- THE ASYMMETRY. A person entitled on the patient's intestacy could not have
-- witnessed the directive (s 3(3)(c)), but is disqualified neither from
-- certifying terminal illness (s 9(9) omits intestacy) nor from acting on the
-- directive (s 10(4) omits it too). The same interest, treated three ways.
#ASSERT NOT `the witness is competent under section 3(3)` (Witness WITH `who` IS `Wong, aged 45`, `is a medical practitioner` IS TRUE, `is the patient's own or chosen practitioner` IS TRUE, `interests` IS `only an intestacy entitlement`)
#ASSERT NOT `section 9(9) disqualifies the practitioner from certifying` `a practitioner entitled only on intestacy`
#ASSERT NOT `section 10(4) disqualifies the practitioner from acting` `a practitioner entitled only on intestacy`

§§ `10(6) -- the pregnancy override`

`the patient is pregnant` MEANS ActingSituation WITH
    `the directive` IS `a directive properly witnessed`
    `the determination` IS `both opinions agree`
    `the practitioner` IS `a specialist`
    `reasonable ground to believe a notice of revocation has been received or sent` IS FALSE
    `reasonable ground to believe the patient communicated an intention to revoke` IS FALSE
    `reasonable ground to believe the patient could not understand the directive when made` IS FALSE
    `ascertained from the Registrar that the directive is registered and in force` IS TRUE
    `ensured the patient has been certified terminally ill under section 9` IS TRUE
    `determined and certified whether the patient is pregnant` IS TRUE
    `the patient is known to the practitioner to be pregnant` IS TRUE
    `it is probable the foetus will develop to the point of live birth with continued treatment` IS TRUE

-- The duty under s 10(2) survives; it is the withholding that s 10(6) forbids.
#ASSERT `the practitioner has a duty to act in accordance with the directive` `the patient is pregnant`
#ASSERT `section 10(6) forbids withholding treatment` `the patient is pregnant`
#ASSERT NOT `the practitioner may lawfully act on the directive` `the patient is pregnant`

§§ `5(3) -- an unregistered directive`

`an unregistered directive` MEANS Directive WITH
    `the patient` IS `Tan, aged 70`
    `in the prescribed form` IS TRUE
    `first witness` IS `Dr Chua, the patient's own doctor`
    `second witness` IS `a lay witness aged 45`
    `the witnesses were present at the same time` IS TRUE
    `registered under section 5` IS FALSE
    `revoked under section 7` IS FALSE

-- Valid under s 3, and still unlawful to act on: s 5(3) is a separate gate.
#ASSERT `the directive was made in accordance with section 3` `an unregistered directive`
#ASSERT `section 5(3) forbids acting on the directive` `an unregistered directive`
